  "notes": [
    "Medians/p95 use only observed values, including failed cases; missing values stay null.",
    "p95 uses linear interpolation. n<20 is flagged; small samples are descriptive only.",
    "Times are monotonic client arrivals and manifest speech boundaries at 32 ms packet submission granularity, not physical microphone or separately measured STT/model delays.",
    "t_speech_end is the LAST cue speech endpoint, distinct from the full sequence end. First-event offsets can be negative for multi-cue/correction sequences.",
    "Request workflow is first audio frame through confirmation; setup includes pairing. No TTS generation time is included.",
    "Usage is a proxy, not provider billing: submitted PCM seconds, websocket-open seconds, HTTP-2xx intent responses (including clarify), and observed final transcripts. Unobserved upstream calls/retries and request-mode intermediate finals are unknown.",
    "Exact structured identifiers are scored. Location aliases, if supplied, are explicit verbatim ground truth; raw literal location checks remain recorded. References and all websocket events remain in JSONL for manual review.",
    "Monitor coverage requires a final transcript and the full window (or expected voice stop). This cannot prove all model calls or the latest interpretation completed; negative outcomes require an offline server-trace cross-check.",
    "Expected correction scores absence of surviving wrong alerts. Safe suppression does not imply a semantic correction or retraction was observed; those are separate."
